!Proposed definitions

;__jo'u__ (JOI): And. Joins two sumti into one sumti. The referents of the resulting sumti are the referents of both sumti considered jointly.

;__fa'u__ (JOI): Respectively. Joins two sumti into one sumti. The referents of the resulting sumti are the referents of both sumti considered jointly and distributively in correspondence with another term.

;__joi__ (JOI): Non-distributive group. Joins two sumti into one sumti. The referents of the resulting sumti are the referents of both sumti considered jointly and non-distributively.

;__ce__ (JOI): Set. Joins two sumti into one sumti. The referent of the resulting sumti is the set whose members are the referents of both sumti considered jointly.

;__ce'o__ (JOI): Sequence. Joins two sumti into one sumti. The referent of the resulting sumti is the sequence whose members are the referents of both sumti considered jointly.

;__jo'e__ (JOI): Union of sets. Joins two sumti into one sumti. The referent of the resulting sumti is the set which is the union of the sets referred to by each sumti.

;__ku'a__ (JOI): Intersection of sets. Joins two sumti into one sumti. The referent of the resulting sumti is the set which is the intersection of the sets referred to by each sumti.

;__pi'u__ (JOI): Cross product of sets. Joins two sumti into one sumti. The referent of the resulting sumti is the set which is the cross product of the sets referred to by each sumti.


!!Formal definitions

||
''sumti1'' JOI ''sumti2''

''sumti1'' .e ''sumti2'' me ''sumti1'' jo'u ''sumti2''

''sumti1'' jo'u ''sumti2'' | lo sumji be ''sumti1'' bei ''sumti2''

''sumti1'' jo'u ''sumti2'' | lu'a ''sumti1'' jo'u ''sumti2''
''sumti1'' joi ''sumti2'' | lu'o ''sumti1'' jo'u ''sumti2''
''sumti1'' ce ''sumti2'' | lu'i ''sumti1'' jo'u ''sumti2''
''sumti1'' ce'o ''sumti2'' | vu'i ''sumti1'' jo'u ''sumti2''

''sumti1'' jo'e ''sumti2'' | lo jomsumji be ''sumti1'' bei ''sumti2''
''sumti1'' ku'a ''sumti2'' | lo kuzyterkruca be ''sumti1'' bei ''sumti2''
''sumti1'' pi'u ''sumti2'' | lo pivypilji be ''sumti1'' bei ''sumti2''

''sumti1'' fa'u ''sumti2'' ''sumti3'' fa'u ''sumti4'' ''selbri''
== ''sumti1'' ''sumti3'' ''selbri'' .i ''sumti2'' ''sumti4'' ''selbri''
||

!!Notes

# The definitions given correspond to their use as sumti connectives. Other uses (when they make sense) have yet to be added.
